DevOps Interview Questions at Amazon 

Round 1 – Cloud Architecture & Infra Reasoning (45 mins)
• What’s the impact of misconfigured security groups during a blue/green deployment on ECS?
• Walk us through a secure, multi-AZ ALB setup for a latency-sensitive app.
• Explain what happens internally in a terraform apply across 2 modules with interdependencies.
• The CI pipeline is failing only on Mondays. How do you triage something this bizarre?
• SSM Session Manager stopped working across staging. How would you debug and secure it again?
• What happens in a cross-region S3 replication with a delete marker race condition?
• Lambda hitting cold starts. show 3 ways to fix across runtime, infra, and design.
• Your team switched from ECS to EKS.  how would you explain that to a non-tech stakeholder?
• Walk through how CloudWatch metric math can mislead incident responders if not configured right.
• One-liner: How to list all EC2s not using the latest AMI in all regions?

Round 2 – Fire Drills & RCA Thinking (75 mins)
• Your NAT Gateway bill just spiked 10x. Where do you look first, and how do you fix it permanently?
• You enabled VPC Flow Logs for debugging. Now they’re gone. What misconfiguration caused this?
• SQS FIFO queue is throttling under load. what’s wrong with your producer setup?
• Jenkins deploy pipeline gets stuck at 70% randomly. what’s your observability path?
• ALB health checks pass. But customers get 502 intermittently. What next?
• App rollout to Lambda went fine. But CloudFront shows stale pages. RCA?
• EKS nodes are healthy, and pods are Pending. Simulate a controlled drill for this.
• Route53 failover didn’t trigger during AZ outage. Why?
• RDS failover happened, but the app didn’t recover for 4 minutes. Who do you blame and why?
• AWS Config flagged a critical drift in S3 bucket ACLs. What’s your prevention mechanism?

Round 3 – Engineering Judgment & Ownership (30 mins)
• How do you push back when PMs prioritize velocity over resiliency?
• Your teammate pushed infra to prod on a Friday evening. What now?
• Describe a time you debugged a system where metrics lied.
• How do you onboard a new DevOps hire without overwhelming them with tribal knowledge?
• What’s your chaos checklist before launching a customer-facing product?

💡 TL;DR:
If you haven’t:
1. Debugged NAT bill spikes from rogue VPCs
2. Simulated Route53 + ALB combo failure
3. Recovered Terraform modules post-deletion
4. Survived Friday deploys without a rollback plan
